course: dictionary
lesson: 9754
title: Supervise: watching over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To supervise means to watch over people or an activity and make sure they do things correctly and safely. «Children must be supervised by an adult when swimming, cooking or using tools.» The sentence gives the clue: an adult watches over them, so they stay safe.
explain: To supervise can also mean to be in charge of workers or a job. «At work, a supervisor is in charge.» A supervisor is the person who does the supervising.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Children never touch fireworks without an adult supervising» becomes «without an adult watching over them to keep them safe». It still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: «Supervise» is a verb: supervise, supervises, supervised, supervising.
fact: «Supervision» is the noun for the watching over, and «supervisor» is the noun for the person who does it.
fact: «Supervise» means to watch over people or an activity and make sure they do things correctly and safely.
fact: Phrases to remember: «adult supervision», «under supervision», «supervise the children».
fact: «YouTube's own rules say children under 13 should use YouTube Kids or a supervised account.» Here «supervised» means watched over by someone who keeps an eye on what happens.
exercise: «Children must be supervised by an adult when using tools.» What does supervised mean here? | *Watched over to keep them safe | Given a prize | Forgotten in the classroom | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the person who is in charge of workers. | supervising | *supervisor | supervise | supervised
exercise: «Teachers supervise playtime.» What are the teachers doing? | Playing football with the children | Ringing the bell early | Sleeping on the bench | *Keeping an eye on the children to keep them safe
test: «Swim where it is supervised» means the swimming is | Only for grown-ups | Done in the dark | Free from all rules | *Watched by an adult or lifeguard to keep you safe
test: Mum says, «We need adult supervision for the sparklers.» What does she mean? | The sparklers must be put away forever | The sparklers are too old to use | Only the children may hold them | *An adult must watch over the sparklers to keep everyone safe
exam: Which word completes this sentence? «A ___ watches over the workers and checks their work.» | *supervisor | supervising | supervises | supervise
